  "details": "As the PPI (pixels per inch / cm) increases with each generation of headset, background VRC+ themes for the VRChat UI will appear more and more crummy as the visual limitations of raster become more obvious, see below for a more obvious example that doesn't require a headset.\n\nTexture compression required to keep the VRChat application relatively small show in the UI themes as visible compression artifacts. baking the more abstract themes into vector could potentially solve this issue.\n\nClick the images to see the inevitable (hyperbole) raster disaster.",
